# Claude Code local state (root only, not templates/*/.claude/).
#
# `/.claude/*` and NOT `/.claude/` — git never descends into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a re-include below it is unreachable. v2.2.6 tracks exactly one
# file under it: `.claude/settings.json`, which is what REGISTERS this repo's own
# three git gates. Before v2.2.6 there was no project settings file at all, the
# gates were wired nowhere, and `git commit` completed in 0s against a 58-117s
# **Test** command — the toolkit shipped the config the gates READ
# (PROJECT_CONTEXT.md) without the wiring that makes them RUN.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json

# Gate artifact written by hooks/run-gate.sh. Must be ignored: as of v2.1.5 the
# artifact is keyed on a temp-index `add -A` of the working tree, so an untracked
# .gate/ would fold the previous run's artifact into the next run's tree hash.
/.gate/

# Agent scratch — superpowers SDD working files are never part of the deliverable
/.superpowers/

# Prevent Claude Code from auto-loading template CLAUDE.local.md files
CLAUDE.local.md

# /CLAUDE.md was ignored while it held machine-specific context-mode routing rules.
# As of v2.0-pr5 it holds toolkit facts (layout, gate, invariants) and is tracked.

